# Sample Ooda CLI Spawn Invocations

File: ooda/examples/spawn.oot

## Spawn opm

```sh
ooda opm add foo
ooda opm audit
ooda opm launch --exec foo
```

These all spawn the `opm` binary as a subprocess. The ooda binary does NOT link the opm package. The lookup order is:
1. `$OODACODEX/bin/opm` (if set)
2. `opm` on `$PATH`

## Spawn lsp

```sh
ooda lsp              # stdio mode (the editor case)
ooda lsp request.txt  # one-shot file mode
```

These spawn the `lsp` binary. The stdio is inherited from the ooda process. The editor's stdio flows through to lsp transparently.

## Spawn mcp

```sh
ooda mcp                       # stdio mode
ooda mcp --file request.txt    # one-shot file mode
ooda mcp-merge config.json     # idempotently inject the ooda entry into an agent-tool JSON config
```

These spawn the `mcp` binary.
